# M (QUALIFICATION): the exactness matrix on the TRAFFIC candidate c2-packed-tp4-best-ship (audits OFF, the pinned sampler in the verify trace, every lever on): the same matrix
# that qualified c2-packed-tp4 (M7). The gate driver adds its own extent audit to the arms; the traffic environment is otherwise untouched.
# READ the report: POLICY PASS, four of four concurrent identical to solo, no refuse_round, no idle commit, no audit mismatch, the arms' profile line c2-packed-tp4-best-ship.
# Duration (estimate): 80-120 min. Stop rule: any non-identical arm stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-4 four-seat SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9 is the SHIPPING base B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-4 commit with the candidate profile
# c2-packed-tp4-best-ship baked in as the image's serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its seat count (4). Every job
# serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default.
# qwen_c2_profiles.json's own default stays c2-packed-tp4: only a build that names C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE (B0's one key) bakes anything. A commit that
# changes a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,8192,16384,24576,32768,49152,60000,120000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=512
C2_GATE_JIT=record
